                {
                  "id": "a01",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Service Intervals, Seasonal Planning, And Uptime Strategies",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "anchor": "uptime-strategies"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a02",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Winslow-Gerolamy Motors Limited helps fleets across Ontario develop preventive maintenance schedules that reduce downtime, control operating costs, and extend truck life.",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a03",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For International trucks and Cummins-powered systems, preventive maintenance is one of the most important factors in improving uptime, avoiding unexpected repairs, and maintaining long-term vehicle performance.",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a04",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Preventive Maintenance Matters For Fleets",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "anchor": "why-it-matters"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a05",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Reactive maintenance often leads to unexpected breakdowns, higher repair costs, lost revenue from downtime, and shortened vehicle life.",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a06",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A structured preventive maintenance program helps fleets:",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a07",
                  "type": "bullet-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Identify issues early"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Maintain consistent performance"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Improve fuel efficiency"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Stay compliant with emissions and safety requirements"
                      }
                    ],
                    "variant": "bullets"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a08",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For Ontario fleets, preventive maintenance is especially important due to changing weather conditions, traffic congestion, mixed operating environments, and demanding route schedules.",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a09",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Recommended Service Intervals For International Trucks",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "anchor": "service-intervals"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a10",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Preventive maintenance schedules should be based on engine type, mileage, engine hours, driving conditions, load demands, and overall vehicle use.",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a11",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Typical maintenance intervals may include:",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a12",
                  "type": "bullet-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Oil and filter changes every 15,000 to 25,000 km"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Fuel filter replacement every 25,000 to 40,000 km"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Air filter inspection and replacement every 40,000 to 80,000 km"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Coolant system service every 12 to 24 months"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Transmission service according to OEM recommendations"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "DPF inspection as part of every regular preventive maintenance cycle"
                      }
                    ],
                    "variant": "bullets"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a13",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "These intervals should always be adjusted based on actual vehicle use and operating conditions.",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a14",
                  "type": "buttons",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "label": "Request service",
                        "url": "/service#service-request",
                        "style": "primary"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a15",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Customizing Maintenance Schedules For Fleet Operations",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "anchor": "customizing"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a16",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "No two fleets operate the same way. Maintenance schedules should reflect the way trucks are actually used in the field.",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a17",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "We help fleets build service plans based on:",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a18",
                  "type": "bullet-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Regional or long-haul route patterns"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Stop-and-go driving and idle time"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Load weight and application demands"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Seasonal weather exposure"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Engine performance and fuel efficiency trends"
                      }
                    ],
                    "variant": "bullets"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a19",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "This helps ensure that service timing is based on real-world conditions rather than generic schedules alone.",
                    "width": "full"
